Force the textarea input path on Android: Chromium EditContext drops IME
selection deletes (Gboard backspace over a selection arrives as a textupdate
that nativeEditContext#_emitTypeEvent maps to type(''), a no-op). See
microsoft/vscode#202787.

2026-07-22 re-check (prune pass): mechanism re-verified on device - without this
patch the Android editor activates NativeEditContext (a native-edit-context DIV);
with it the textarea path is used. The behavioural repro was inconclusive on
Chrome 134: a selected word becomes a Gboard composing region, so its backspace
removes one character rather than exercising the selection-replace no-op. This is
a browser-version-dependent Chromium defect and current Chromium (151/152) will
not run under the x86_64 emulator's ARM translation, so kept. Retest the Gboard
backspace-over-selection on a physical device with current Chrome before deleting.

diff --git a/lib/vscode/src/vs/editor/browser/config/editorConfiguration.ts b/lib/vscode/src/vs/editor/browser/config/editorConfiguration.ts
--- a/lib/vscode/src/vs/editor/browser/config/editorConfiguration.ts
+++ b/lib/vscode/src/vs/editor/browser/config/editorConfiguration.ts
@@ -144,8 +144,11 @@
 			outerHeight: this._containerObserver.getHeight(),
 			emptySelectionClipboard: browser.isWebKit || browser.isFirefox,
 			pixelRatio: PixelRatio.getInstance(getWindowById(this._targetWindowId, true).window).value,
+			// Android IMEs delete a non-empty selection via a textupdate that
+			// nativeEditContext maps to a no-op type(''), so backspace over a
+			// selection is silently dropped; the textarea path handles it.
 			// eslint-disable-next-line local/code-no-any-casts, @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
-			editContextSupported: typeof (globalThis as any).EditContext === 'function',
+			editContextSupported: typeof (globalThis as any).EditContext === 'function' && !browser.isAndroid,
 			accessibilitySupport: (
 				this._accessibilityService.isScreenReaderOptimized()
 					? AccessibilitySupport.Enabled
